  "retestHistory": [
    "Focused authoring found unsupported line ends reapplied to an input in a mixed selection by the later text-style patch. Both patch paths now use the same geometry filter; the original failing assertion was retained.",
    "Independent review found empty closed contours affecting earlier open contours, rounded native outlines rebuilt as squares, hidden-side paint leakage, and slanted-bar vertex ordering. Product fixes retain the original geometric constraints and have regression coverage.",
    "The first desktop harness compared serialized SVG attribute order. It now compares canonical name/value attributes; all values and geometric checks remain.",
    "Visual review and a failing red-gradient endpoint pixel check found transformed arrow groups sampling the wrong paint coordinates. Each endpoint now compensates its gradient transform; preview and offline pixel regressions pass.",
    "The first complete production browser run passed 197 of 208 cases; 11 old selectors became ambiguous after fill/stroke separation. Semantic layer selectors retain exact geometry, color and width assertions. The original report and targeted 11/11 rerun are retained separately; both existing line runtime workflows now include gradient-endpoint pixel regressions."
  ]
